      "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=26, \\\\ b & =AC=22, \\\\ m∠A & ={11}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{11}^{∘}=0.190\\,809,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 22\\cdot 26\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{11}^{∘} \\\\  & =286\\cdot (0.190\\,809) \\\\  & ≈54.57,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
